const group = [
{
"id":"Q06",
"source_passages":[{"section":"Scoring / Victory Conditions; Dominance (3.3)","quotation":"**Dominance (3.3):** In own Daylight at **at least 10 VP**, activate a dominance card from hand into play area; remove score marker and stop scoring VP. Cannot remove/replace activated card. At **start of own Birdsong**, win if ruling **three clearings of matching mouse/rabbit/fox suit**, or for **bird dominance, two diagonally opposite corner clearings**. Meeting condition earlier does not immediately win. Dominance cards cannot be crafted, but can be spent for suit. Whenever one would enter discard, put it near map available instead. During own Daylight, spend matching card to take available dominance into hand. Available **bird dominance remains bird**, so payment must be bird; a bird hand card can pay for non-bird dominance. Activation and taking are separate, neither requires a faction action allowance."}],
"answer":[{"part":"Spent dominance and taking an available card","ruling":"When a dominance card would enter the discard pile, place it near the map as an available card instead. During your own Daylight, spend a matching card to take an available dominance card into your hand; taking it does not activate it. An available bird dominance card remains bird, so it requires a bird card as payment. A bird card may pay to take a non-bird dominance card.","evidence":"Scoring / Victory Conditions; Dominance (3.3)"}],
"support":"supported",
"evidence":["Scoring / Victory Conditions; Dominance (3.3)"]
},
{
"id":"Q07",
"source_passages":[
{"section":"Setup; Standard Setup (Law 5.1)","quotation":"Use **Standard Setup**, in this order (Law 5.1):\n\n1. Choose factions; determine starting player and seating randomly. Take faction boards and their listed pieces. Use Fall or Winter. Fall has no special rules; on Winter, the river divides forests just as printed paths do. Rivers are otherwise not paths.\n2. Put score markers at 0.\n3. With two players, remove all four dominance cards. Shuffle shared deck; each player draws **three cards**.\n4. **Ruins and items:** Cover the four R building slots with ruins. The separate map item supply is **2 boots, 2 bags, 1 crossbow, 1 hammer, 2 swords, 2 tea, 2 coins**. Keep the four R-marked ruin items separate from this supply: only Vagabond faction setup hides one each of its R-marked bag, boot, hammer and sword beneath the four ruins, **one item beneath each ruin**. During that Vagabond setup, shuffle the ruin/item stacks and return each to an empty R ruin slot, keeping item identities hidden. Without a Vagabond, ruins contain no items.\n5. The map item supply uses its corresponding spaces near the top of the map.\n6. Distribute overview cards as desired; put battle dice nearby.\n7. Set up factions in their letter order: Marquise, Eyrie, Alliance, Vagabond. Setup order is distinct from turn order."},
{"section":"Setup; Hidden ruin items (only when Vagabond is present, during its faction setup)","quotation":"**Hidden ruin items (only when Vagabond is present, during its faction setup):**\n\n1. Take the four ruins and R-marked bag, boot, hammer and sword. Put **one item beneath each ruin**.\n2. **Shuffle the ruin/item stacks**, keeping identities hidden.\n3. **Return each stack to an empty R ruin slot** on the map. With no Vagabond, leave the four ruins without hidden items."}
],
"answer":[
{"part":"Two-player deck and hand","ruling":"Remove all four dominance cards before shuffling the shared deck; each player draws three cards.","evidence":"Setup; Standard Setup (Law 5.1)"},
{"part":"Ruins and items","ruling":"Cover the four R building slots with ruins. Keep the map supply separate: 2 boots, 2 bags, 1 crossbow, 1 hammer, 2 swords, 2 tea and 2 coins, placed in corresponding map spaces. Only if Vagabond is included, put one each of its R-marked bag, boot, hammer and sword beneath the four ruins, shuffle the ruin/item stacks to hide identities, and return one stack to each empty R slot. Without Vagabond, the ruins have no hidden items.","evidence":"Setup; Standard Setup (Law 5.1), Hidden ruin items"},
{"part":"Faction setup order","ruling":"Set up factions in letter order: Marquise, Eyrie, Alliance, then Vagabond. This setup order does not determine turn order.","evidence":"Setup; Standard Setup (Law 5.1)"}
],
"support":"supported",
"evidence":["Setup; Standard Setup (Law 5.1), Hidden ruin items"]
},
{
"id":"Q08",
"source_passages":[
{"section":"Marquise de Cat (6); Keep and Field Hospitals","quotation":"**Keep:** Only Marquise may **place** pieces in its clearing; other players may **move** pieces into it. The keep cannot be placed again if removed. **Field Hospitals:** Whenever any number of Marquise warriors are removed from a clearing, Marquise may spend one card matching that clearing to place those warriors in the keep clearing instead of supply. This can apply outside battle. Without a keep there is no destination for hospitals. See **FAQ & Rulings** for Hospitals during an ambush at the Keep."},
{"section":"FAQ & Rulings; Field Hospitals during an ambush at the Keep","quotation":"- **Field Hospitals during an ambush at the Keep:** Marquise may spend a matching card immediately when its warriors are removed, returning them to the Keep clearing **before** checking whether the ambush left no attacking warriors or pawns. If returned warriors remain there, battle continues. Without Hospitals, battle ends if no attackers remain after the ambush. (FAQ under 4.3.1 and 6.2.3.)"}
],
"answer":[
{"part":"Keep placement and rebuild","ruling":"Only the Marquise may place pieces in the Keep clearing; other players may move pieces into it. If the Keep is removed, it cannot be placed again.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Keep and Field Hospitals"},
{"part":"Field Hospitals, including ambush at the Keep","ruling":"Whenever any number of Marquise warriors are removed from a clearing, Marquise may spend one card matching that clearing to place those warriors in the Keep clearing instead of returning them to supply; this can happen outside battle. If the Keep is absent, Hospitals have no destination. During an ambush at the Keep, the matching card may be spent immediately as warriors are removed, returning them before the check for whether attackers remain; if returned warriors remain there, battle continues. Without Hospitals, if no attackers remain after the ambush, battle ends.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Keep and Field Hospitals; FAQ & Rulings"}
],
"support":"supported",
"evidence":["Marquise de Cat (6); Keep and Field Hospitals","FAQ & Rulings; Field Hospitals during an ambush at the Keep"]
},
{
"id":"Q09",
"source_passages":[{"section":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight actions","quotation":"**Daylight:** First craft with workshops. Then take **up to three actions**, plus **one per bird card spent outside an action**, in any order and number except Recruit's limit:\n\n- **Battle:** One battle.\n- **March:** Up to two moves; either may use the same or different warriors. Do not interrupt the compound action to spend a bird card or take another action.\n- **Recruit:** One warrior at **each recruiter**; only **once per turn**. If supply cannot fill all recruiters, place maximum available, choosing among eligible recruiters.\n- **Build:** Choose a clearing you rule with open slot and choose building type. Take the leftmost building of that type. Pay cost shown atop its column by removing that many wood from the target clearing or from other ruled clearings linked to it through an unbroken chain of ruled clearings. Place building; score VP on uncovered space. You cannot build without full wood cost, the building and legal slot.\n- **Overwork:** Spend a card matching a sawmill's clearing to place one wood there."}],
"answer":[
{"part":"Daylight order and allowance","ruling":"First craft with workshops. Then take up to three actions, plus one action per bird card spent outside an action. Actions may be in any order and number, subject to Recruit's once-per-turn limit.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight actions"},
{"part":"March","ruling":"One March action allows up to two moves, using the same or different warriors. The compound action cannot be interrupted to spend a bird card or take another action.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight actions"},
{"part":"Recruit","ruling":"Recruit once per turn: place one warrior at each recruiter. If supply cannot fill every recruiter, place the maximum available and choose among eligible recruiters.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight actions"},
{"part":"Overwork","ruling":"Spend a card matching the clearing of a sawmill to place one wood there.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight actions"}
],
"support":"supported",
"evidence":["Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight actions"]
},
{
"id":"Q10",
"source_passages":[{"section":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight Build action","quotation":"- **Build:** Choose a clearing you rule with open slot and choose building type. Take the leftmost building of that type. Pay cost shown atop its column by removing that many wood from the target clearing or from other ruled clearings linked to it through an unbroken chain of ruled clearings. Place building; score VP on uncovered space. You cannot build without full wood cost, the building and legal slot."}],
"answer":[{"part":"Build procedure","ruling":"Choose a clearing you rule that has an open building slot, then choose the building type and take the leftmost building of that type from its track. Pay the cost shown atop that type's column by removing that amount of wood from the target clearing or from other clearings you rule that connect to it through an unbroken chain of ruled clearings. Place the building and score the VP shown on the newly uncovered track space. Building is not legal unless the full wood cost, building piece and legal slot are available.","evidence":"Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight Build action"}],
"support":"supported",
"evidence":["Marquise de Cat (6); Daylight Build action"]
}
